<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109375" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποτομ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a cutting off below,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.980c
			</span></i>; <i>cutting away underneath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.2.7
			</span></i>, Heliod ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				45.6.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Leonid.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				7.71
			</span></i>: pl., <i>trimmed surfaces</i> of blocks of stone in
			architecture, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.3073.113
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				114
			</span></i> (Lebad., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a smaller incision</i> or <i>line,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Hyp.</u>
				3.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποτομῆς μόριον</span>”
				<i>sub-division,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theol.Ar.
					4
				</span></i>
			. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
			<i>null and void, rescinded,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				5(2).344.14
			</span></i> (Orchom. <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
			</span></i>, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
